The episode also paid reference to a big classic
who episode Planet of the Spiders from the

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:18.890
Third Doctor’s Run.

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:22.750
I feel like everyone is going to have a lot
to say about Clara after they get a chance

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:23.750
to see it.

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:32.460
Really good news too, The Doctor Who Legacy
people gave me a game code to add to my giveaway.

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:34.580
I’ll explain how that works at the end,
but the regular weekly giveaway is still running.

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:39.870
All you have to do to enter is be a subscriber
and leave a comment. So two different giveaways

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:40.870
this week.

00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:46.090
Spider Time, Top 5 Moments. careful for spoilers
if you haven’t seen the episode yet. I’ll

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:49.580
wait just a sec...okay, here we go.

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:55.920
Number 5 - Mothballing The Shuttle Program
Bites The United States In The Ass

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:59.541
I am a huge space geek and a huge NASA geek,
so back in 2011 when they ended the Space

00:00:59.541 --> 00:01:01.240
Shuttle Program I was super pissed. I understand
it’s a money thing, and I don’t want to

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:05.719
talk politics and military spending but I
was so happy that Doctor Who wagged it’s

00:01:05.719 --> 00:01:07.470
finger at the whole thing.

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:12.380
The whole episode was a cautionary tale about
the value of the Space Program in every country.

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:16.890
The United States just teamed up with India
to explore Mars, so the lesson isn’t totally

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:21.780
lost. But you get the idea. Ignore Space at
the peril of hatching moon creatures.

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:26.330
Mexico deserves a high five for spending the
money to build a mining operation on the moon

00:01:26.330 --> 00:01:30.240
too. It sucks they didn’t find any minerals,
but when the moon is really an egg there’s

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:31.450
nothing you can do about it.

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:35.840
I just love that they literally had to pull
the space shuttle out of a museum and fix

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:37.530
it to go back to space.

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:41.380
In reality right now, the United States and
other countries that want to go to the International

00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:43.330
Space station typically use Russia’s Space
Program.

00:01:43.330 --> 00:01:45.310
There is a lot of international cooperation
just because spaceflight is so expensive.

00:01:45.310 --> 00:01:48.990
Number 4 - The Doctor Takes Courtney to the
Moon to Make Her Feel Special

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:53.770
It’s really hard to tell how seriously he
took fixing Courtney and Clara’s feelings

00:01:53.770 --> 00:01:57.880
in the episode. I’ll talk about Clara in
a sec, she’s a whole different story.

00:01:57.880 --> 00:02:01.060
What was going on with Courtney was that the
Doctor wasn’t trying to be mean, he was

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:19.440
off-handedly dismissing her.

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:23.580
I felt like the comments he made at the end
of the episode implied that the female president

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:25.140
was supposed to be Courtney.

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:28.481
There’s some logic issues with that but
the timeline is about right. Courtney would

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:33.930
be about 48 years old but she’s British,
so she’d be the Prime Minister, not the

00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:35.790
President.

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:40.700
I took issue with Clara at the end of the
episode, even if the doctor was being callous

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:48.130
in his treatment of them. He’s not there
to make your decisions for you.

00:02:48.130 --> 00:02:54.700
And he totally delivered on Courtney, she
walked away being the first woman to walk

00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:59.540
on the moon’s surface and she probably grows
up to become the prime minister or someone

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:00.730
amazing.

00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:15.519
Courtney was awesome in this episode, Clara

00:03:15.519 --> 00:03:18.340
was not.

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:21.459
Number 3 - The Doctor Can’t See Fixed Moments
In Time

00:03:21.459 --> 00:03:25.830
I don’t think this was giant foreshadowing
for the finale or anything. The Doctor has

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:27.510
made this same comment many times before.

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:31.460
He’s not lying, there are always going to
be moments in time he can’t see clearly.

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:36.360
But the key word is “Clearly” he still
has an idea for what could happen and he can

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:39.620
make deductions based on all the available
information.

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:42.940
The thing that confused me a little was when
they were on the beach watching the creature

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:48.190
hatch and he had that speech about humanity
spreading itself to the stars. He seemed really

00:03:48.190 --> 00:03:49.190
sad.

00:03:49.190 --> 00:03:52.540
I wonder if he was thinking about the events
of Utopia and The Sounds of Drums.

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:56.220
Where, in the very very far future the Master
tricks the last living humans into becoming

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:58.180
the Toclafane.

00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:00.000
Number 2 - Planet of The Spiders

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:04.080
The Spiders were really a small part of the
episode but it was a nice reference to the

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:06.940
Third Doctor’s last story Planet of the
Spiders.

00:04:06.940 --> 00:04:10.250
At the end of that he regenerated into the
Fourth Doctor so not only was it really creepy

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:14.110
because giant spiders, it was also a big moment
in Doctor Who history.

00:04:14.110 --> 00:04:18.359
I loved that Courtney was able to neutralize
them with Windex. It’s funny sometimes how

00:04:18.359 --> 00:04:24.800
Doctor Who as a series will take a lot of
care in teasing big things, then just throw

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:26.569
them away.

00:04:26.569 --> 00:04:29.840
All the promos for the episode made you think
these spiders were going to be the big challenge

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:34.349
but they were just a a smudge on the window
of the TARDIS. Nothing a little windex won’t

00:04:34.349 --> 00:04:35.349
fix.

00:04:35.349 --> 00:04:37.749
and my Number 1 moment - The Moon is an Egg

00:04:37.749 --> 00:04:41.699
They were very non-specific about what kind
of creature it was, the Doctor just says it’s

00:04:41.699 --> 00:04:46.639
the only one of it’s kind. But it is capable
of fertilizing it’s own eggs. So I can reproduce.

00:04:46.639 --> 00:04:50.389
They just have a gestation period of 100 Million
Years.

00:04:50.389 --> 00:04:55.800
There was actually a Star Trek Next Generation
Episode where they did a giant Space Baby.

00:04:55.800 --> 00:04:59.699
The enterprise has to help it hatch and then
it imprints, thinking the ship is it’s mother.

00:04:59.699 --> 00:05:04.050
That would be kind of funny if a space baby
thought the TARDIS was it’s mother.

00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:11.319
The TARDIS is alive too, but technically it
doesn’t reproduce, it grows like a tree.

00:05:11.319 --> 00:05:14.889
That would be fun to watch, watch a TARDIS
being born or grown or however you want to

00:05:14.889 --> 00:05:15.889
think about it.

00:05:15.889 --> 00:05:19.479
That’s what we need for the next big Doctor
Who Anniversary. We need a scene on Gallifrey

00:05:19.479 --> 00:05:23.629
where we get to watch TARDISes being built.
Somebody start a letter writing campaign to

00:05:23.629 --> 00:05:27.080
Moffat.

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:31.319
Let me know what your favorite moment was,
the tumblr jokes, the Moon Hatching?

00:05:31.319 --> 00:05:34.490
This was one of my more favorite episodes
so far.

00:05:34.490 --> 00:05:37.520
Here’s a few of the better references I
spotted. If there’s any you saw just write

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:38.520
them in the comments.

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:42.930
First was the Neil Armstrong Speech Courtney
Woods did, One Giant Leap for a Thingy Thing.

00:05:42.930 --> 00:05:47.240
Who needs to pay attention in history class,
definitely not Courtney.

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:51.629
The Doctor uses a Yo-Yo that looks just like
the one Tom Baker always played with. He used

00:05:51.629 --> 00:05:57.379
it to test gravity but Peter Capaldi uses
it to save Courtney.

00:05:57.379 --> 00:06:00.619
There was something of a geronimo moment when
the Doctor lept over the cliff, he didn’t

00:06:00.619 --> 00:06:04.080
say it but I feel like we were all thinking
it.

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:13.800
then there was all the tumblr. This was great.
The official Doctor Who team has one of the

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:18.029
biggest accounts on Tumblr. They interact
with the fandom there more than any other

00:06:18.029 --> 00:06:21.429
social media platform.

00:06:21.429 --> 00:06:26.360
But I feel like the doctor yelling at courtney
about posting pictures of him was a reference

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:28.379
to all the leaked pictures from the set.

00:06:28.379 --> 00:06:31.809
There were actually a lot of pictures from
this episode of them filming on the beach

00:06:31.809 --> 00:06:33.189
in the space suits. I think he was referencing
those, along with all the other leaked pictures

00:06:33.189 --> 00:06:34.189
from this year.

00:06:34.189 --> 00:06:35.189
Let me know if you spotted any other big references.

00:06:35.189 --> 00:06:41.149
Overall I gave the episode an A minus, The
story was really grand and I love how it connected

00:06:41.149 --> 00:06:46.969
several big moments in Doctor Who history,
between the third doctor and the toclafane.

00:06:46.969 --> 00:06:57.969
Courtney Woods acquitted herself nicely, I
know 

00:06:57.969 --> 00:07:02.800
a lot of you weren’t huge fans of her last
week but Clara was really the person I didn’t

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:04.020
like in this episode.

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:09.279
I feel like she’s forgetting who the Doctor
really is. They blur the lines a lot between

00:07:09.279 --> 00:07:14.369
Capaldi being a total alien and being her
best friend. Deep Breath made it explicit

00:07:14.369 --> 00:07:16.879
that The Doctor was not here for our amusement.

00:07:16.879 --> 00:07:22.940
And he’s not here to make decisions for
us. So watching Clara get upset and cry like

00:07:22.940 --> 00:07:24.689
a baby wasn’t fun.

00:07:24.689 --> 00:07:27.669
I feel like she’s not learning, maybe that
will change in a future episode. But eventually

00:07:27.669 --> 00:07:29.959
she has to come to the conclusion that The
Doctor is not an all powerful god watching

00:07:29.959 --> 00:07:31.839
over her. She has to learn to take responsibility
for her choices.

00:07:31.839 --> 00:07:36.090
You can’t get mad at someone when all they
promised you was an adventure, the doctor

00:07:36.090 --> 00:07:39.469
never promises you won’t die.

00:07:39.469 --> 00:07:44.400
Definitely a great episode, I’m really wondering
what Danny Pink’s really bad day was about.

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:48.009
We will definitely learn about that, so don’t
worry.

